solution.en:
A model answer. Every expected value comes from the contract, and the arithmetic is shown in the comments.

import org.junit.jupiter.api.Test;
import static org.junit.jupiter.api.Assertions.*;

class DiscountTest {
    @Test
    void typicalDiscount() {
        // discount = 1000 * 25 / 100 = 250, pays 750
        assertEquals(750, Main.discounted(1000, 25));
    }

    @Test
    void rateZeroChangesNothing() {
        assertEquals(100, Main.discounted(100, 0));
    }

    @Test
    void rateHundredIsFree() {
        assertEquals(0, Main.discounted(100, 100));
    }

    @Test
    void discountRoundsDown() {
        // discount = 5 * 50 / 100 = 2.5, rounded down to 2, pays 3
        assertEquals(3, Main.discounted(5, 50));
        // discount = 99 * 10 / 100 = 9.9, rounded down to 9, pays 90
        assertEquals(90, Main.discounted(99, 10));
    }

    @Test
    void tinyPriceWithBigRate() {
        // discount = 1 * 99 / 100 = 0.99, rounded down to 0, pays 1
        assertEquals(1, Main.discounted(1, 99));
    }

    @Test
    void freeItemStaysFree() {
        assertEquals(0, Main.discounted(0, 50));
    }

    @Test
    void negativePriceIsRejected() {
        assertThrows(IllegalArgumentException.class, () -> Main.discounted(-1, 10));
    }

    @Test
    void rateAboveHundredIsRejected() {
        assertThrows(IllegalArgumentException.class, () -> Main.discounted(100, 101));
    }

    @Test
    void negativeRateIsRejected() {
        assertThrows(IllegalArgumentException.class, () -> Main.discounted(100, -1));
    }
}

Why these tests: a good set follows the contract. The typical case checks the main formula. The rates 0 and 100 are the boundaries of the allowed range, where off-by-one mistakes live. The rounding tests use values where cents * rate is not a multiple of 100, because only then does the rule "rounded down" matter. The invalid inputs sit just outside the range: -1 for the price, -1 and 101 for the rate, which are the first bad values on each side.

Notes: assertEquals takes the expected value first, which matters for the failure message. Each test checks one idea, so a failure points at one cause. Deriving expected values by running the code would only prove that the code agrees with itself.

solution.zh:
参考答案。每个预期值都来自契约，计算过程写在注释里。

import org.junit.jupiter.api.Test;
import static org.junit.jupiter.api.Assertions.*;

class DiscountTest {
    @Test
    void typicalDiscount() {
        // 折扣 = 1000 * 25 / 100 = 250，应付 750
        assertEquals(750, Main.discounted(1000, 25));
    }

    @Test
    void rateZeroChangesNothing() {
        assertEquals(100, Main.discounted(100, 0));
    }

    @Test
    void rateHundredIsFree() {
        assertEquals(0, Main.discounted(100, 100));
    }

    @Test
    void discountRoundsDown() {
        // 折扣 = 5 * 50 / 100 = 2.5，向下取整为 2，应付 3
        assertEquals(3, Main.discounted(5, 50));
        // 折扣 = 99 * 10 / 100 = 9.9，向下取整为 9，应付 90
        assertEquals(90, Main.discounted(99, 10));
    }

    @Test
    void tinyPriceWithBigRate() {
        // 折扣 = 1 * 99 / 100 = 0.99，向下取整为 0，应付 1
        assertEquals(1, Main.discounted(1, 99));
    }

    @Test
    void freeItemStaysFree() {
        assertEquals(0, Main.discounted(0, 50));
    }

    @Test
    void negativePriceIsRejected() {
        assertThrows(IllegalArgumentException.class, () -> Main.discounted(-1, 10));
    }

    @Test
    void rateAboveHundredIsRejected() {
        assertThrows(IllegalArgumentException.class, () -> Main.discounted(100, 101));
    }

    @Test
    void negativeRateIsRejected() {
        assertThrows(IllegalArgumentException.class, () -> Main.discounted(100, -1));
    }
}

为什么选这些测试：好的测试集合要紧扣契约。普通情形检查主要公式。费率 0 和 100 是允许范围的边界，差一错误就出在那里。取整测试选用 cents * rate 不是 100 的倍数的值，因为只有这时“向下取整”这条规则才起作用。非法输入紧贴范围之外：价格取 -1，费率取 -1 和 101，它们是两侧第一个不合法的值。

说明：assertEquals 的第一个参数是预期值，这会影响失败时的提示信息。每个测试只检查一个想法，所以失败时能指向一个原因。如果通过运行代码来得到预期值，只能证明代码与它自己一致。

